"For each item below, fetch its source and check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item. A card item is a field of the plan in the producer's words, with the sources it cites: check each factual claim in it against those sources, and any value it carries against the page; what the plan will build, measure or predict needs no source, but a factual claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED. For a cost input, check that the page states the number for the setting given; whether it applies to this plan is not yours to judge. When the page states a different number for a num or rate item, give it as page_value. Decide only from the pages you fetch and the text below; do not read files. Return one status per item, under its ref: SUPPORTED, PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED or UNREACHABLE, with the page sentence you relied on.
Items, one per line:
{\"ref\":\"card:question\",\"text\":\"Can concurrent CPU docking jobs reduce complete workflow cost while preserving every output across four fixed cases?\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:hypothesis\",\"text\":\"Concurrent independent jobs may fill idle CPU capacity, reducing workflow time without changing docking calculations or retained poses.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_lever\",\"text\":\"Width 2 or 4 preserves outputs and achieves at least 1.05 speed factor in both repeats against nearby original serial blocks.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_not\",\"text\":\"Widths 2 and 4 preserve outputs but fail the 1.05 speed-factor threshold in at least one repeat each.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:test_summary\",\"text\":\"Compare original four-case serial run, four separate serial jobs, and 2 or 4 concurrent jobs, keeping 26 threads per job. Require identical outputs and nearby original serial times divided by concurrent times >=1.05 in both repeats. Allocation time limit costs $6.58 before tax.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:closest_prior\",\"text\":\"MEGADOCK reported 98% scaling at 420 heterogeneous nodes; it did not test fixed-thread CPU job concurrency on one host. [prior]\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"prior\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4221127/\",\"quote\":\"Notably, a high scalability (98%) was obtained with the largest number of nodes (420 nodes).\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:left_open\",\"text\":\"Whether widths 2 or 4 preserve every output and exceed 1.05 speed factor twice on one fixed host.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:anchor\",\"text\":\"Reproduce frozen CPU docking records and every retained pose exactly; then verify separate serial units against fresh original execution.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:limits\",\"text\":\"CPU scheduling screen only; no GPU acceleration, dense-search recovery, biological efficacy, population generalization or confidence claim from two repeats.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"src:prior\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4221127/\",\"quote\":\"Notably, a high scalability (98%) was obtained with the largest number of nodes (420 nodes).\",\"supports\":\"Published heterogeneous-node scaling result; different resource axis and workload from this single-host scheduling calibration. Search returned article text; subsequent direct opening encountered browser verification.\"}

Return only one JSON value, with no other text, that matches this JSON Schema:
{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"description\":\"One entry per item sent, with its ref unchanged.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"ref\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"\\"card:<field>\\", \\"src:<source id>\\", \\"num:<number id>\\" or \\"rate:<rate id>\\", as sent.\"},\"status\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"SUPPORTED\",\"PARTIAL\",\"UNSUPPORTED\",\"CONTRADICTED\",\"UNREACHABLE\"]},\"page_quote\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The text on the page this status rests on.\"},\"note\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"page_value\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"num and rate items: the value the page states.\"}},\"required\":[\"ref\",\"status\",\"page_quote\",\"note\"]}}},\"required\":[\"items\"]}"
